{"seq":7,"slug":"special-inclusive-education","title":"特殊教育与全纳教育","stage":"DONE","category":"education","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/education/special-inclusive-education","rating":{"composite":3.66,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.6,"coverage":3.5,"positioning":3.5,"strategic":4},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"特殊教育与全纳教育\">特殊教育与全纳教育</h1><p>我第一次认真想到这个领域，是因为意识到一个问题：学校究竟是为「平均的那个孩子」设计的，还是为「所有孩子」设计的。一旦你接受后者，你就被迫重新思考课程、评估、教室布局、师资分工乃至法律——这正是特殊教育与全纳教育这门学科要回答的。它不是「给残障学生开小灶」，而是关于如何让教育系统对人的差异本身保持友好。</p>\n<p>这个 hub 把整片领域拆成四条由浅入深、互相咬合的主线，按从「为什么」到「怎么做」的顺序展开。</p>\n<p>第一条主线是<strong>基础</strong>。我们先问：什么叫全纳，它和早期的「隔离安置」「随班就读」差在哪里？接着追问一个更底层的问题——我们到底怎么理解「残障」这件事。是把它看成个体身上需要修复的缺陷（医学模型），还是看成环境与社会制造的障碍（社会模型）？这个看似抽象的分歧，会一路决定后面所有的评估方式和支持策略。最后，基础部分落到法律与权利：从美国的 IDEA、《康复法》第 504 条，到联合国《残疾人权利公约》第 24 条，再到中国的随班就读政策，权利不是口号，而是可被起诉、可被问责的制度。</p>\n<p>第二条主线是<strong>评估与干预</strong>，回答「怎么知道一个孩子需要支持，又怎么把支持落到实处」。这里有三个核心装置：科学、无偏见的鉴别与评估；作为法律文件和教学蓝图的个别化教育计划（IEP）；以及不必等孩子「失败到够格」才介入的多层支持系统（RTI/MTSS）。三者构成一条从发现、规划到分层响应的闭环。</p>\n<p>第三条主线是<strong>障碍类别</strong>。这里不堆砌诊断标签，而是挑出实践中最高频、也最容易被误解的几类——学习障碍与注意缺陷多动障碍、自闭症谱系、以及智力、发展性与感官障碍——讲清它们的成因、表现，以及对应的循证支持。理解类别是为了更精准地支持，而非为了贴标签。</p>\n<p>第四条主线是<strong>实践与前沿</strong>，把前三条主线收束到日常教室。通用学习设计（UDL）让我们从一开始就为差异而设计，而不是事后补救；辅助技术——尤其是 2026 年迅速成熟的 AI 工具——正在重新定义「可及」的边界；全纳实践与家校社协作则提醒我们，没有任何一个老师能独自完成全纳，它本质上是一项协作工程。</p>\n<p>四条主线的递进逻辑是：先建立价值观与法律地基，再学会发现与规划，然后理解具体的人，最后落到可执行的教学与协作。读完整个 hub，你应当能回答一个贯穿始终的问题——如何让「每个学习者平等受教育」从理想变成可操作的日常。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations","title":"基础","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/education/special-inclusive-education/foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"intro-and-inclusion-philosophy","title":"特殊教育导论与全纳理念","url":"/l-doc-books/h/education/special-inclusive-education/foundations/intro-and-inclusion-philosophy"},{"seq":2,"slug":"models-of-disability","title":"残障的模型与分类","url":"/l-doc-books/h/education/special-inclusive-education/foundations/models-of-disability"},{"seq":3,"slug":"law-policy-rights","title":"法律、政策与权利","url":"/l-doc-books/h/education/special-inclusive-education/foundations/law-policy-rights"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"assessment-intervention","title":"评估与干预","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/education/special-inclusive-education/assessment-intervention","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"identification-assessment","title":"鉴别与评估","url":"/l-doc-books/h/education/special-inclusive-education/assessment-intervention/identification-assessment"},{"seq":2,"slug":"individualized-education-plan","title":"个别化教育计划（IEP）","url":"/l-doc-books/h/education/special-inclusive-education/assessment-intervention/individualized-education-plan"},{"seq":3,"slug":"response-to-intervention-mtss","title":"干预反应模型与多层支持（RTI/MTSS）","url":"/l-doc-books/h/education/special-inclusive-education/assessment-intervention/response-to-intervention-mtss"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"disability-categories","title":"障碍类别","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/education/special-inclusive-education/disability-categories","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"learning-disabilities-adhd","title":"学习障碍与注意缺陷多动障碍","url":"/l-doc-books/h/education/special-inclusive-education/disability-categories/learning-disabilities-adhd"},{"seq":2,"slug":"autism-spectrum","title":"自闭症谱系","url":"/l-doc-books/h/education/special-inclusive-education/disability-categories/autism-spectrum"},{"seq":3,"slug":"intellectual-developmental-sensory","title":"智力、发展性与感官障碍","url":"/l-doc-books/h/education/special-inclusive-education/disability-categories/intellectual-developmental-sensory"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"practice-frontiers","title":"实践与前沿","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/education/special-inclusive-education/practice-frontiers","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"universal-design-differentiation","title":"通用学习设计（UDL）与差异化教学","url":"/l-doc-books/h/education/special-inclusive-education/practice-frontiers/universal-design-differentiation"},{"seq":2,"slug":"assistive-technology","title":"辅助技术","url":"/l-doc-books/h/education/special-inclusive-education/practice-frontiers/assistive-technology"},{"seq":3,"slug":"inclusive-practice-collaboration","title":"全纳实践与家校社协作","url":"/l-doc-books/h/education/special-inclusive-education/practice-frontiers/inclusive-practice-collaboration"}]}]}